<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Geist Fonts Example</title>
  <style>
    @font-face {
      font-family: 'GeistMonoVF';
      src: url('GeistMonoVF (1).woff') format('woff');
      font-weight: normal;
      font-style: normal;
    }

    @font-face {
      font-family: 'GeistVF';
      src: url('GeistVF.woff') format('woff');
      font-weight: normal;
      font-style: normal;
    }

    body {
      background-color: #fafafa;
      color: #222;
      padding: 40px;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    h1 {
      font-family: 'GeistVF', sans-serif;
      font-size: 3rem;
      margin-bottom: 0.5em;
    }

    p {
      font-family: 'GeistVF', sans-serif;
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      margin-bottom: 1em;
    }

    code {
      display: block;
      background-color: #272727;
      color: #00ff90;
      padding: 16px;
      border-radius: 10px;
      margin-top: 30px;
      font-family: 'GeistMonoVF', monospace;
      font-size: 1.1rem;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Geist Fonts Demo</h1>
  <p>This paragraph uses the GeistVF variable font.</p>
  <p>The code block below uses GeistMonoVF, great for monospaced code examples:</p>
  <code>
    function greet() {<br>
    &nbsp;&nbsp;console.log('Hello, Geist!');<br>
    }
  </code>
</body>
</html>
